From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:16:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 571/571] [V2] Copy drafts in the runner: wide verification and
 the copy state's report

The runner sizes verification (request drafts, rejection and greedy
verification, adaptive verification, the sink, the sampler and structured
output rows, the kernel declarations) for num_verification_tokens; the
speculator keeps DSpark's block. After DSpark drafts, the copy drafter
replaces a copying request's drafts and confidences; adaptive verification
keeps them with the planned confidences a later step's budget reads (one
buffer, one TP broadcast; a new request's rows reset), and the async output
carries the copy allocation to the scheduler. Block verification of a step
where no request was scheduled more than DSpark's block runs its TileLang
kernels at the block's width into the lookahead's output (kernel_steps), so
DSpark's steps run the kernels they ran before. The warmup decodes one request
at the lookahead and the rest at the block, as the scheduler lays them out.
test_tilelang_rejection.py reruns at VLLM_TEST_VERIFICATION_STEPS=16.
